   "text": "This is a maleimidocaproyl\u2011Val\u2011Cit\u2011PABC\u2011MMAF\u2011type drug\u2011linker. I read it left to right in the drawing.\n\n1. **Maleimide and linker:** a maleimide ring (2,5\u2011dioxopyrrole) is attached through N to a five\u2011CH2 chain ending in an amide C=O (the caproyl group).\n2. **Val\u2011Cit:** the caproyl C=O acylates the N of valine (isopropyl side chain, drawn with a wedge). Valine is followed by citrulline, whose side chain is (CH2)3\u2011NH\u2011C(=O)NH2. The citrulline centre is drawn with plain bonds, so I gave it no stereo.\n3. **PAB spacer:** citrulline's C=O forms an anilide with a para\u2011substituted benzene. The benzene carries CH2\u2011O\u2011C(=O)\u2011 at the other end, a carbamate.\n4. **N\u2011methyl valine:** the carbamate N carries a methyl and a valine residue.\n5. **Valine:** the next residue is valine, joined by an amide.\n6. **Dolaisoleuine:** its N is methylated. It bears a sec\u2011butyl group and a CH(OMe)CH2C(=O) unit, which acylates the proline N.\n7. **Dolaproine:** the pyrrolidine ring carries CH(OMe)\u2011CH(CH3)\u2011C(=O)\u2011NH.\n8. **Phenylalanine:** the chain ends in a phenylalanine with a free CO2H.\n\nFor stereochemistry I took the standard MMAF/MMAE configurations for the peptide, dolaisoleuine and dolaproine centres. I re\u2011derived each @/@@ for the atom order I wrote. The Val, N\u2011Me\u2011Val and Phe centres are assigned as L from the usual convention rather than read off individual wedges.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)NC(CCCNC(N)=O)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2[C@H](OC)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)O)cc1"
  }
